 184:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c **** /**
 185:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****    * @brief  Update SystemCoreClock variable according to Clock Register Values.
 186:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         The SystemCoreClock variable contains the core clock (HCLK), it can
 187:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         be used by the user application to setup the SysTick timer or configure
 188:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         other parameters.
 189:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           
 190:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   * @note   Each time the core clock (HCLK) changes, this function must be called
 191:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         to update SystemCoreClock variable value. Otherwise, any configuration
 192:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         based on this variable will be incorrect.         
 193:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *     
 194:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   * @note   - The system frequency computed by this function is not the real 
 195:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           frequency in the chip. It is calculated based on the predefined 
 196:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           constant and the selected clock source:
 197:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *             
 198:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSI, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSI_VALUE(*)
 199:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *                                              
 200:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSE, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(**)
 201:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *                          
 202:frameworks/f407/Core/Src/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is PLL, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(**) 
